.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
generated
**/generated
.turbo
coverage
**/coverage
*.log

# Uploaded files: they live in a volume at runtime (see docker-compose), so
# baking the local ones into the image would only ship stale files — including
# other people's receipts.
apps/backend/uploads

# Secrets: never bake these into an image layer.
#
# The `**/` variants are NOT redundant: a bare `.env` pattern matches ONLY the
# context root, so apps/backend/.env, apps/web/.env and packages/database/.env
# would all be copied in — JWT_SECRET and NEXTAUTH_SECRET included. Every
# service gets its real values at RUNTIME via env_file/environment in
# docker-compose, so nothing needs them at build time.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
